orname{arcsin}⁡(x):$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/df22eea4331c47da3047381ca672fd80ebf75118054316fe88c0e2d96dae0d34.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)$ is $x\\in [-1,1].$  \n\nNow, substituting $x=0$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,0}(2x\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)) & =2\\cdot 0\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-152757/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f458c61-bc51-5653-9ecb-1e96eb5c335e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-152757"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339131/field-1/928df4272a89a0432586f410fc807f5a62e3c25172b3a66adba64b089a2aa458" :answer/id #uuid "8bf337a8-b5a4-5a83-81db-d81ff85a0333" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3+\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339131/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "53222422-9b67-56e6-a4ab-c741881611f0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339131/field-1/928df4272a89a0432586f410fc807f5a62e3c25172b3a66adba64b089a2aa458" :answer-field/choices ["q-339131/field-1/928df4272a89a0432586f410fc807f5a62e3c25172b3a66adba64b089a2aa458"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339131" :question/id #uuid "9ad685fe-8879-588e-8c60-0099d11bdb00" :question/math-academy-id "q-339131" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\sqrt{3}/2}(2\\sqrt{3}x+6\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x):$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/85a182aabfe64c27eaafde94e3bdbede9409b02cfd87395cb2fc5543b09c4e05.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)$ is $x\\in [-1,1].$   \n\nNow, substituting $x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ directly into the limit, we have  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\sqrt{3}/2}(2\\sqrt{3}x+6\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)) & =2\\sqrt{3}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})+6\\cdot \\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =3+6\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =3+\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339131/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f458c61-bc51-5653-9ecb-1e96eb5c335e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339131"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-152804/selection/e0bd991ac2e2f2a23ec920e03c6d5103be6b20c12a25d724ab290d4ba5292c3e" :answer/id #uuid "d830f0f0-ca80-5598-948a-75ecc06df018" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152804/selection/d6f27b7c7939a102723fed67409856455f84c69bf3e5c2599003ca6bf26244df" :answer/id #uuid "16f10d8d-aea1-5d45-ae42-fb83850398c8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Undefined" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152804/selection/d0ab94490dee12664d2f70471811316d5faf74c9c2c3f6dde546976ea292b76b" :answer/id #uuid "2c5e5b2b-3ea5-575a-87e0-50975db2f3b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152804/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "f205aa08-d49d-5ee0-9ba0-7ef458d8fae6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152804/selection/75d4bf82dfc61c34c77bbbf7bd5b3bd55806108bbef22fc9bcd32571f4f3b0b8" :answer/id #uuid "ebc48fde-e5f6-542a-ba01-2e35b421cc11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152804/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4133f92f-6aae-55c9-9f09-9a13186434c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-fiel