(\\frac{x+1}{2})?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x+1}{2}):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/922781004fc917f3a62726689c43f0226c680de58f446b741f9994c4c65134e3.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x+1}{2})$ is $x\\in [-3,1].$ This means that $\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x+1}{2})$ is undefined outside this interval.\n\nTherefore, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }8\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x+1}{2})$ is undefined." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-152869/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4bcc5d54-e7fd-5be5-9d00-4240d03e21cb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-152869"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339330/field-1/82a873b6b3ece3b4059b2da1839886387bbd4d4e56d0ad136fc169204f9d3030" :answer/id #uuid "c09bf845-0c17-56ce-91e4-ed1095c438c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339330/field-1/e7e505d325c3cadeeeaf26a0afda20aaa10bea508f9739931632d1057683cd77" :answer/id #uuid "750c8ae8-5259-5d94-92ff-f9c084bf81f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339330/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "be1245d4-cc61-52d9-8325-23f44a77d608" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339330/field-1/82a873b6b3ece3b4059b2da1839886387bbd4d4e56d0ad136fc169204f9d3030" :answer-field/choices ["q-339330/field-1/82a873b6b3ece3b4059b2da1839886387bbd4d4e56d0ad136fc169204f9d3030" "q-339330/field-1/e7e505d325c3cadeeeaf26a0afda20aaa10bea508f9739931632d1057683cd77"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339330" :question/id #uuid "0ca39296-785a-5b9f-bd41-07df813f9b3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-339330" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }(\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x+1))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x+1):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/e441953c2cefc6f817a64cb7ce0ebce53164ebb4d3974ae871b14d57450b5167.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x+1)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Moreover, from the graph, we see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x+1)=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }(\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x+1))=\\pi -(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339330/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4bcc5d54-e7fd-5be5-9d00-4240d03e21cb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339330"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343225/field-1/15220adc03cfdd78909df30c93eaa6db3dfe4c4cb0891a395cb4f082cc959c85" :answer/id #uuid "4ad1c79d-f1c3-5b56-a24c-dd0e0b90c60f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343225/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac724ebb-cd59-502f-a052-2b91ec57f710" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343225/field-1/15220adc03cfdd78909df30c93eaa6db3dfe4c4cb0891a395cb4f082cc959c85" :answer-field/choices ["q-343225/field-1/15220adc03cfdd78909df30c93eaa6db3dfe4c4cb0891a395cb4f082cc959c85"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343225" :question/id #uuid "0777d39c-5dbc-502d-832a-4a2d915f8b68" :question/math-academy-id "q-343225" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }(10\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x+3))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x+3):$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/bb49c052cabe12e8869270ab61b1de9e7f45b6acd6eaa9bc0d4c6892446a7cb6.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x+3)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Moreover, from the graph, we see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x+3)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }(10\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x+3))=(10\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})=5\\pi .\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343225/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4bcc5d54-e7fd-5be5-9d00-4240d03e21cb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343225"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-152890/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "4c8c5cb1-143c-5819-9abf-b855d8e43d9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152890/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "4b935fc7-e380-5114-9e52-0215a4878d92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152890/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "1cc0b939-946e-50e3-9f15-0b30a3a84de7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152890/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer/id #uuid "23d16969-d38b-5bc3-9961-b8ecdc223bd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152890/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "b8b78d40-84e8-5131-9ee1-6b308e050d71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152890/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "73062c0b-1bb1-5675-b20d-b02fcea42f5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-152890/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-152890/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-152890/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-152890/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" "q-152890/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" "q-152890/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-152890" :question/id #uuid "5a8abbc2-0426-5776-9148-d32d6510319e" :question/math-academy-id "q-152890" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x))=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/ca5e8035505f20619b6707d6d1f2d0b7b2f125a004a0dbd9d448840b0e4ffd99.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)$ is $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nAs $x$ increases to $\\infty ,$ the graph tends to $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-152890/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a58f115-f368-5171-af73-37084085b42a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-152890"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339500/field-1/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer/id #uuid "cb0c7a81-7641-59c0-9233-16662e5f0148" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339500/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "cb4f3204-1b07-538d-b8d1-8339a35f8fe0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339500/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "627bffb8-8132-5eb6-8964-5eecd1ce4523" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339500/field-1/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer-field/choices ["q-339500/field-1/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" "q-339500/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339500" :question/id #uuid "b3afa35b-eeeb-5afa-aaf1-a5819291da16" :question/math-academy-id "q-339500" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x+1))=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/f5cef3bda76e80edfa467a90823c9b6ad6aca1f8a5e8e3e06dc585258e975e0a.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x+1)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nAs $x$ increases to $\\infty ,$ the graph tends to $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x+1)) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-339500/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a58f115-f368-5171-af73-37084085b42a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339500"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-344578/field-1/a05724295bc0340162295da21b8749cd336584b7c76ed9f6810ddb03e7f98d00" :answer/id #uuid "ad5e7de2-2dc0-5fd1-b9b6-4c9adab8f1be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344578/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e3e65d8-f16e-521d-b9f5-3912eedae649" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344578/field-1/a05724295bc0340162295da21b8749cd336584b7c76ed9f6810ddb03e7f98d00" :answer-field/choices ["q-344578/field-1/a05724295bc0340162295da21b8749cd336584b7c76ed9f6810ddb03e7f98d00"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344578" :question/id #uuid "c4dfd88c-8fd0-5fa6-a390-4f040e6c68f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-344578" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\sqrt{3}}tan\\,(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/ca5e8035505f20619b6707d6d1f2d0b7b2f125a004a0dbd9d448840b0e4ffd99.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $x=\\sqrt{3}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\sqrt{3}}tan\\,(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =tan\\,(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-344578/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a58f115-f368-5171-af73-37084085b42a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-344578"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-149958"] :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to \\,-1/2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x))=$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/9dcc5a116c2a564547283783a7df7b1cd3a9ab3b76ac24dc2695c4cb367796d5.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)$ is $x\\in [-1,1].$  \n\nNow, substituting $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-1/2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-302690/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "2f1cdfa3-e161-5c97-9a8f-c0c88c352ad1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-302690/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "547b70b6-5a17-574a-87a0-e699a471d542" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-302690/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-302690/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-302690" :question/id #uuid "53aec58a-1622-5fa5-804d-afee9e1d5fc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-302690" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/fc06a4e63f38a315dd3944f65f871cca2dbdddee26ec268e857f79e5f4ab8848.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)$ is $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nAs $x$ increases to $\\infty ,$ the graph tends to $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2\\pi ) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-302690/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a58f115-f368-5171-af73-37084085b42a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-302690"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-10535"] :question/problem "Evaluate $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to 0} \\dfrac{\\arccos(x) -\\pi}{x-\\pi}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\arccos(x){:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/9dcc5a116c2a564547283783a7df7b1cd3a9ab3b76ac24dc2695c4cb367796d5.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\arccos(x)$ is $x \\in [-1,1].$  \n\nNow, substituting $x=0$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)-\\pi }{x-\\pi }) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(0)-\\pi }{0-\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\pi )}{(-\\pi )} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{(-\\pi )} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-10536"] :question/problem "What is the value of $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to \\, \\infty} \\arccos(x-1)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y = \\arccos(x-1){:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/4ccf7e79e19f49027f615a075e655139e6926b3ba30fe35d63078fd7917d8869.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\arccos(x-1)$ is $x \\in [0,2].$ This means that $\\arccos(x-1)$ is undefined outside this interval.\n\nTherefore, $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to \\, \\infty} \\arccos(x-1)$ is undefined." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-10537"] :question/problem "Compute the value of $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to \\, \\infty}\\cos\\left( \\dfrac{2}{3}\\arctan \\left(2x+1\\right)\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of  $y =\\arctan \\left(2x+1\\right){:}$  \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/06d01e3eb47f69e5172e0ba3c99708a05c79b12a48764fe29c50e94f93b73dd1.png)\n\nThe domain of   $\\arctan \\left(2x+1 \\right)$ is $(-\\infty,\\infty).$   \n\nAs $x$ increases to $\\infty,$ the graph tends to $y={\\color{blue}\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x+1)) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
